WEBVTT

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.490
So this is the city of Tokyo...

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.010
What a beautiful place.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:05.980
<b>My Talent Is Being a Scarecrow</b>

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:15.700
I was sure the place I'm staying 
was right around here,

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.360
but I don't see a building 
that looks like it...

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.320
Hey, look.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:26.020
That girl has chicks on her head.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:27.710
How cute!

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:32.500
Tokyo has so many buildings and 
train tracks, it's like a maze...

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.210
What's the matter, miss?

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:37.280
Are you lost?

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:39.700
There are a lot of 
dead-end streets in this area.

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:41.700
Wh-Wh-Wh-What should I do?

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:42.930
That's a big bag. Did you just move to Tokyo?

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:42.930
I-I...

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:45.680
Are you a student? Is the place 
you're heading to near here?

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:48.070
<i>Wh-Which question should I answer first?</i>

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:48.980
Oh, by the way, that restaurant 
has great Russian cuisine.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:52.860
Come to think of it, when 
my daughter came here yesterday,

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:52.860
<i>No, maybe I should introduce myself first...</i>

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:56.360
she got lost and had a pretty rough time.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:57.340
<i>I'd better not say anything that 
would offend someone from Tokyo...</i>

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:24.010
A scarecrow?

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:29.020
Once again, I wasn't able to speak well.

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:33.770
I've always been bad at talking, 
so I've practiced a lot, but...

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:37.900
Hello, tanukis, bunnies, birds!

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:42.010
Which story should I read today?

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:44.460
Do you like Cinderella?

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:48.530
Animals sure do love you, Hina-chan.

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:51.910
That keeps the birds out of my fields, 
so I appreciate it.

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:54.170
I don't even need a scarecrow anymore.

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:55.420
U-Um...

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:00.160
Oh, my! You froze up!

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:02.130
You look just like a scarecrow.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:06.850
For some reason, I was always 
being put to work as a scarecrow.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:11.140
I finally got into the 
high school of my dreams.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:14.000
I want to at least try to 
not freeze up in front of people,

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:17.150
<b>-Japanese
There's a quiz tomorrow
We covered most of it yesterday
-PE is basketball, 
so prepare gym shoes</b>

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:17.150
<b>-We're going to be doing oil painting in art, 
so wear clothes and an apron that can get dirty
Preparations are necessary, 
so get to the art room early</b>

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:17.150
and be able to talk easily with others.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.970
And while I was worrying about that, 
I made it here...

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:29.990
<b>Used Bookstore 
Hitotose</b>

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:29.990
This is where I'm staying?

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:33.500
I'm pretty sure
 it's the right address, but...

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.760
That employee is so pretty.

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:50.260
Is she reading?

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:57.520
Or... eating?

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:02.640
Can I help you?

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:04.900
U-Um...

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:06.410
Um, I...

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:10.410
I was told that I could stay here...

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:11.200
Oh!

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.700
You're Hinako-chan, right?

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:15.210
The landlady's told me all about you!

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:16.800
The second floor is used for apartments.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:18.990
That's where I live, too.

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:20.130
Um... I...

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.710
My name's Kuina.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:24.720
I'll go get the landlady!

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:28.720
<b>-Thank you for letting me borrow the textbook yesterday!
-The book I borrowed is inside the desk.
-Sorry I couldn't return it to you in person.
-You're a lifesaver!</b>

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:28.720
<b>-If you ever need anything let me know.
-Thank you so much!
Lets hang out again!</b>

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:37.020
Some of these books look so old.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:40.240
This shop has such a nice atmosphere.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:42.980
<b>In the Forest, Under Cherries in Full Bloom 
Sakaguchi Ango</b>

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:56.250
Sorry, it looks like 
the landlady's out right now...

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:01.220
Why won't you look me in the eye?

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:04.170
I've never seen someone 
eating a book before...

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:06.760
That was... um...

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:09.510
I love reading,

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:11.760
and books are basically my friends.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:14.520
I adore them so much, I want to eat them up.

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:17.770
<i>D-Don't eat your friends!</i>

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:21.400
A-Anyway, I'll show you to your room.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:23.680
This room is yours.

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:30.410
What a beautiful room!

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:33.170
It's like I'm in a hotel!

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:36.160
A chest with its own atmosphere,

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:38.390
a cute bed...

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:40.670
and even a maid!

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:42.790
Wait... a maid?

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:44.170
Oh?

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:47.170
<i>Wh-Why is there a maid in my room?</i>

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:50.180
Nice to meet you. I'm Mayuki.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:51.130
Huh?

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:53.540
I live and work here.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:54.760
You can call me Mayu.

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:57.730
You live here?

00:06:57.730 --> 00:06:59.730
She's a resident here.

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:03.330
All residents work here. That's the rule.

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:06.530
Schoolwork comes first, though, 
so it's only on weekends.

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:08.420
I see!

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:11.260
So that's why Mayu-chan is a maid?

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:12.490
No.

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:15.620
I'm an employee in the coffee shop.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:17.940
This is just what I always wear.

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:19.820
Huh? They're your own clothes?!

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:24.370
I-I heard that someone new 
was moving in today,

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:26.500
so I was just cleaning up this room!

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:29.630
Mayu-chan wants to be a princess. Right?

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:31.560
You like frills.

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:32.970
N-No, I don't!

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:34.970
Don't treat me like a child!

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:38.570
I'm just rehearsing for when I'm 
invited to dances in the future,

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:41.350
so I won't step on the hem of my dress!

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:43.680
<i>She's like a child...</i>

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:46.900
Hina-chan, you're starting at 
Fujimiya High in spring, right?

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:49.430
I'm so glad I'll have a kouhai there now!

00:07:49.430 --> 00:07:51.480
Huh? A kouhai?

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:54.760
Did you think I was a first-year like you?

00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:56.370
I may not look it, but I'm a second-year!

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:57.530
I'm sorry!

00:07:57.530 --> 00:08:01.910
People always think I look younger than I am.

00:07:58.390 --> 00:08:01.910
<i>I can't tell her I thought 
she was in elementary school...</i>

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:04.880
But don't worry, it doesn't bother me.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:07.540
By the way, I'm a first-year, too.

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:08.670
So we'll be together.

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:11.470
Yeah! I'm looking forward to it!

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:14.970
The toilet is in the middle of the hallway.

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:19.720
We only have a given amount of time 
to use the bath, so be careful of that.

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:24.230
Kuu-chan, that's immodest!

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:25.610
Bad!

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:28.980
Well, I didn't finish my breakfast...

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:31.360
Oh, all right.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:34.610
It's noon, anyway. Why don't we have lunch?

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:36.030
In a bookstore?

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:37.380
Nope.

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:44.000
See? This is the coffee shop where I work.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:45.540
You're right!

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:48.500
<b>Coffee shop</b>

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:48.500
<b>Used Bookstore</b>

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:48.500
<b>You Are Here</b>

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:48.500
There's a coffee shop 
in the back of the bookstore!

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:52.260
Here, Hina-chan.

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:53.760
Take this.

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:55.010
Huh?

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:59.510
I have to eat a book, too?

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.140
This is a menu.

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:05.270
Oh, so it is.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:10.290
Why did you enroll at our 
high school, Hina-chan?

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:10.690
Huh?

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:14.350
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:16.660
<i>Where should I start explaining?</i>

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:21.170
Well... when I was a scarecrow 
out in the country...

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:22.950
Huh? A scarecrow?

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:25.470
You mean those dolls that stand in fields?

00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:27.510
What did you do?

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:30.790
She froze up...

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:33.420
She really does look like a scarecrow.

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:39.430
<b>Today's practice menu
-Stretches <-- Do them properly!
-3 kilo marathon <-- Try your best not to walk
-Vocal exercises
-Review the script</b>

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:39.430
<b>-Review strong and weak points 
and check on props
-Check on costume
</b>

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:36.080
I wondered what exactly she did.

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:39.430
So she literally freezes up 
and does nothing...

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:43.770
As you can see, I get nervous easily...

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:46.890
It's unusual to see someone become 
a scarecrow because of nerves.

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:50.180
But during my school's field trip last year,

00:09:50.180 --> 00:09:52.520
I saw a theater club play here.

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:56.680
I was so moved by the 
actors' bold performances.

00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:00.910
I wanted to be like that, too.

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:11.420
So I decided I wanted to be in theater, too.

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:15.200
And that's why you enrolled 
at our high school?

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:18.930
Um, are you two in theater or anything?

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:21.240
You're both really cute,

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:23.970
and I bet Kuu-chan could write good stories.

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:27.600
And Mayu-chan could play 
a princess, maybe...

00:10:28.070 --> 00:10:31.860
I'd probably eat the script 
right after writing it...

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:33.860
Really?

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:37.860
I could never wear a dress! 
I'd be too embarrassed!

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:41.150
<i>But that outfit doesn't embarrass her?</i>

00:10:41.150 --> 00:10:44.530
So you're going to join 
the theater club, then?

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:45.600
Yeah.

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:48.120
Our school is pretty prestigious.

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:51.060
I want to be able to talk a lot 
in front of people,

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.060
Huh?

00:10:51.060 --> 00:10:54.630
and I want to make lots of friends, too.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:57.180
Good luck!

00:10:57.180 --> 00:10:58.760
I'm rooting for you!

00:10:58.760 --> 00:10:59.970
Thanks!

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:03.260
I heard the theater club was 
shut down last year, though.

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:04.790
Oh, yeah, come to think of it...

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:05.970
You're kidding!

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:15.980
I didn't hear about that!

00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:20.860
I know it's my fault for not checking 
before I enrolled there, but...

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:24.870
But, but... there was no Internet 
out in the country!

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:27.990
And I just bought that cell phone yesterday!

00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:38.420
I'm going to join the theater club!

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:43.920
I'm not interested in any other clubs,

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:46.810
and I'm not good at any sports or arts...

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:50.810
Good at... The only thing I'm good at is...

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:54.310
...being a scarecrow, I guess.

00:11:56.210 --> 00:12:00.690
Scarecrows wouldn't be 
of any use in Tokyo, would they?

00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:03.730
I almost forgot.

00:12:03.730 --> 00:12:08.050
If I'm going to live here, I have to work.

00:12:08.050 --> 00:12:09.700
Which means...

00:12:11.090 --> 00:12:13.990
W-Welcome.

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:17.120
No way, no way! I could never do that!

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:18.460
Hina-chan?

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:19.840
What's wrong?

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:21.510
Why were you yelling?

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:24.840
S-Sorry! It was nothing!

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:28.510
<b>Tears</b>

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:31.350
<b>Family Photo</b>

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:31.350
Hina-chan, are you...

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:33.480
...homesick?

00:12:34.210 --> 00:12:36.020
I'm sorry I didn't notice!

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:36.530
Uh...

00:12:36.530 --> 00:12:38.860
Of course. You just moved to Tokyo.

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:39.750
H-Huh?

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:42.500
Want to go out for a change of pace?

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:45.230
There's a big park nearby.

00:12:45.230 --> 00:12:47.800
Really? A park?

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:51.120
There's lots of greenery there, 
too. I'm sure you'll like it.

00:12:51.460 --> 00:12:54.280
There's a place near there 
that has great chicken skewers,

00:12:54.280 --> 00:12:56.640
and a stand that has great dumplings, too.

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:58.540
And also ice cream...

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:02.380
No description of the actual park, huh?

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:06.130
Kuu-chan, are you hungry again?

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:14.890
Once we're on this road, 
it's straight ahead.

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:18.270
Oh, the café there has amazing cakes!

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:21.780
Hey, come on. We just ate lunch.

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:24.780
And once we turn this corner...

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:27.280
<b>Taiyaki</b>

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:27.280
Hey! Kuu-chan, not there!

00:13:27.810 --> 00:13:31.780
Honestly, you're so easily tempted by food.

00:13:31.780 --> 00:13:35.790
Sorry... I smelled delicious taiyaki, 
so I couldn't help myself.

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:38.090
Don't blame me if you get lost.

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:40.670
You're like an older sister, Mayu-chan.

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:44.420
<i>An older sister...</i>

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:46.800
Taiyaki...

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:52.070
H-Honestly, Kuu-chan, 
you're hopeless without me.

00:13:52.070 --> 00:13:53.810
W-Wait here, okay?

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:57.190
Your big sister will go buy taiyaki for you.

00:13:57.460 --> 00:13:59.090
Yay!

00:13:59.090 --> 00:14:01.020
When did she become our big sister?

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:06.840
Mister, I'd like three taiyaki, please.

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:09.530
Sure thing.

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:13.760
And since you're such a cutie, 
I'll give you a discount.

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:15.750
Thank you!

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:19.060
Here you go.

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:24.210
<b>Taiyaki</b>

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:21.280
She's so cute...

00:14:24.690 --> 00:14:26.900
He gave me a discount!

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:29.780
She was our big sister a minute ago,

00:14:29.780 --> 00:14:32.550
and now she's an elementary schooler.

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:38.500
So sweet!

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:39.990
Yum!

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:43.480
It's crispy on the outside,

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:47.230
with lots of soft red bean paste 
on the inside.

00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:50.990
Actually, I think this is the first time 
I've bought food and eaten it on the spot.

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:53.740
Hina-chan, are you heading home?

00:14:54.340 --> 00:14:55.990
Want some watermelon?

00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:59.030
Hup... hup...

00:15:00.490 --> 00:15:03.000
Here's a fresh-picked tomato and cucumber.

00:15:03.660 --> 00:15:05.320
I'll throw in a daikon, too.

00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:06.000
Um...

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:08.680
<i>I got most of my food for free...</i>

00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:10.010
Aren't these great?

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:17.000
See? Here it is.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:20.890
It's so big!

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:27.030
And the cherry trees are in bloom—

00:15:31.400 --> 00:15:32.990
U-Um...

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.540
<b>I met a kitty cat in town today
It kept meowing
and kept calling to me, so I followed it, 
and ended up at a gathering spot for kitties!</b>

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.540
<b>There were a lot of cute kitties, 
and they all came up to me 
and were friendly.
I was so happy.</b>

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:47.310
Hina-chan, have you calmed down?

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:50.550
Yeah. Sorry I worried you.

00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:54.770
Not many people come 
over this way, so you can relax.

00:15:54.770 --> 00:15:56.340
Too bad...

00:15:56.930 --> 00:16:00.690
The dumplings from the stand 
by the entrance were so good, too.

00:16:00.690 --> 00:16:04.440
Darn it, Kuu-chan! 
Get your mind off food already!

00:16:05.140 --> 00:16:07.690
She can eat more?

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:10.450
Can we go look at the ducks?

00:16:10.450 --> 00:16:11.620
Ducks?

00:16:13.050 --> 00:16:14.200
It's true!

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.320
There are ducks in the pond!

00:16:16.610 --> 00:16:18.790
How cute!

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:21.830
Stare...

00:16:22.580 --> 00:16:24.290
<i>She couldn't be...</i>

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:28.840
I won't eat the duck.

00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:36.360
U-Uh... Kuu-chan, do you like ducks?

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:39.720
Yeah! Especially the way 
they slide through the water...

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:42.850
It looks so cool, like a stealth fighter!

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:45.350
Uh... S-Ste...?

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:50.610
What do you think? Isn't it a nice place?

00:16:50.930 --> 00:16:54.490
All the greenery reminds me 
of the forests out in the country.

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:56.890
I was feeling a bit down,

00:16:56.890 --> 00:16:58.290
but I feel better now.

00:16:58.290 --> 00:16:59.370
That's great.

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:01.750
I guess you're not homesick anymore.

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:03.550
Homesick?

00:17:03.550 --> 00:17:04.710
Who did it?!

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:08.750
Who killed my friend with this blade?!

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:10.410
Identify yourself at once!

00:17:10.410 --> 00:17:11.760
Who are those people?

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:14.540
There are lot of small theater 
troupes around here,

00:17:12.790 --> 00:17:16.900
The killer couldn't have been 
someone here. Can't you see that?

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:19.270
so the aspiring actors and troupe members 
come here to practice often.

00:17:16.900 --> 00:17:21.000
You're wrong! The door to this 
place was closed the whole time!

00:17:19.270 --> 00:17:21.000
Wow...

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:22.930
Aren't they cool?

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:23.880
And the windows lock from the outside.

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:26.310
They look like they're running 
straight toward their dream.

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:26.310
Nobody could've gotten in or out.

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:30.730
<i>I really do want to go into theater...</i>

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:31.820
<i>Wait!</i>

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:34.570
That girl practicing over there is Aki-chan!

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:36.320
Hey!

00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:42.740
I wondered why you weren't at home,

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:44.580
but I didn't expect to see you here!

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:46.100
What were you doing?

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:49.630
If you were going out, 
you should have said so.

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:51.250
Vocal practice.

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:55.440
Hina-chan, this is a classmate of mine,

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:57.760
and the landlady of our building.

00:17:57.760 --> 00:17:58.200
Huh?

00:17:58.200 --> 00:18:00.640
Hello. Nice to meet you.

00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:08.600
I'm Chiaki, the landlady of Hitotose Manor.

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:17.820
<i>She's tall and has a nice figure...</i>

00:18:19.750 --> 00:18:21.700
<i>She's so beautiful.</i>

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:25.710
N-Nice to meet you!

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:27.510
I-I'll be in your care starting today.

00:18:27.510 --> 00:18:29.000
I-I'm Hinako.

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:36.420
Looks like an arranged marriage meeting.

00:18:36.790 --> 00:18:40.370
You know, Aki-chan 
used to be a child actress.

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:43.430
She still loves theater to this day.

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:48.130
She used to be in the theater club 
at Fujimiya High School, too.

00:18:48.130 --> 00:18:49.990
She's normally quiet,

00:18:49.990 --> 00:18:52.690
but on the stage, she's a different person!

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:55.060
Her role as a former biker gang member

00:18:55.060 --> 00:18:58.260
and young proprietress at a traditional 
inn who's now an idol singer

00:18:58.260 --> 00:18:59.950
was especially powerful.

00:19:00.380 --> 00:19:02.450
<i>What kind of play was that?</i>

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:04.480
I can't decide...

00:19:09.890 --> 00:19:12.210
I-I...

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:17.210
I entered Fujimiya High School because 
I wanted to be in its theater club.

00:19:17.620 --> 00:19:21.350
But when I heard the club was 
shut down, I was so shocked.

00:19:21.350 --> 00:19:23.430
More accurately, it's on hiatus.

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:25.270
Hiatus?

00:19:26.610 --> 00:19:30.280
The club's advisor is on a theater trip.

00:19:33.470 --> 00:19:35.500
It's on break in the meantime.

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:36.400
What?!

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:38.370
It's on hiatus because of that?

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:40.820
What are the other members doing?

00:19:46.970 --> 00:19:49.330
Just like me,

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:52.570
they're all doing 
the things they want to do.

00:19:53.280 --> 00:19:56.250
O-Oh, no...

00:19:57.690 --> 00:20:01.340
But if you want to perform 
theater that much,

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:03.380
why don't you start a theater troupe?

00:20:03.980 --> 00:20:05.120
Huh?

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:07.720
Small theater troupes 
don't need many members.

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:10.350
So you'd be the leader, Hina-chan?

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:12.600
More accurately, she'd be the principal.

00:20:13.620 --> 00:20:15.060
A theater troupe...

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:16.860
What, what?

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:18.860
What are you guys talking about?

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:22.000
Could I really make one?

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:24.610
You have members. You'd be fine.

00:20:25.300 --> 00:20:25.990
You have four.

00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:26.870
Huh?

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:27.870
Four?

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:31.120
Wait, are we being dragged into something?

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:37.460
<b>Hitotose</b>

00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:44.790
I feel alive again...

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:52.300
So many things happened today.

00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:54.400
I met lots of people,

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:57.040
went to lots of places,

00:20:57.040 --> 00:20:59.910
and experienced lots of firsts.

00:21:00.970 --> 00:21:05.370
I was sad when I heard 
the theater club had been shut down...

00:21:05.370 --> 00:21:06.070
But...

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:09.080
Starting a theater troupe, huh?

00:21:10.010 --> 00:21:13.960
Could I really do something like that?

00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:22.670
Still, all the people at 
Hitotose Manor are so nice.

00:21:23.320 --> 00:21:26.430
I hope everything will work out.

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:28.430
Hina-chan?

00:21:28.430 --> 00:21:31.380
You're been in here 
for a long time. Are you o—

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:38.870
Hina-chan, hang in there! 
Oh, what do I do?!

00:21:38.870 --> 00:21:40.310
Something wrong?

00:21:40.310 --> 00:21:41.790
Get Aki-chan!

00:21:41.790 --> 00:21:43.100
Ah! Hina-chan!

00:21:43.100 --> 00:21:43.580
I'm here.

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:44.980
Whoa! She looks like a boiled octopus!

00:21:44.980 --> 00:21:46.300
What do you mean, "I'm here"?!

00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:47.860
I'm not sure how to answer that.

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:48.840
Hina-chan!

00:21:48.840 --> 00:21:49.730
What's wrong?

00:21:49.730 --> 00:21:51.820
What do we do?!

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:34.680
<b>It Begins Here</b>

00:23:25.720 --> 00:23:29.230
Can I really start a theater troupe?

00:23:29.230 --> 00:23:31.840
I can't be a scarecrow forever.

00:23:31.840 --> 00:23:36.800
I have to remember how I felt on the day 
I decided that's how I wanted to be!

00:23:36.800 --> 00:23:39.110
Next time: "It Begins Here."
